6,"record_id":"MLDB-004695","detection":"ICP-MS","method_description":"The lipophilicity of cinoplatin was determined using the shake-flask method. Briefly, a saturated aqueous solution of cinoplatin was prepared using water presaturated with n-octanol. An aliquot corresponding to ≈50% of this stock solution was then mixed with an equal volume of n-octanol presaturated with water. The resulting biphasic system was stirred at room temperature for 1 h to allow partitioning equilibrium to be established. Phase separation was achieved by centrifugation at 14000 g. The platinum concentration in both the initial and final aqueous phases was quantified by ICP-MS, and the partition coefficient (log PO/W) was calculated using the equation below. logPo/w = log(([C]initial - [C]final)/[C]final)"}]}